import Legal from '../../components/Legal.astro';
---
<Legal
  site="agency"
  title="Refunds & Cancellation — Tisvia Marketing"
  heading="Refunds &amp; cancellation"
  description="How to cancel an engagement with Tisvia Marketing, what notice is needed and what is refundable."
  updated="10 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy covers marketing services provided by Tisvia Marketing. The academy course has its
    own policy on the <a href="https://academy.tisviamarketing.in/refund/">academy site</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Monthly retainers</h2>
  <p>
    Either side may end a retainer with <strong>15 days' written notice</strong>, by email to the
    address below. The current month is worked and billed in full. We hand over reports, assets and
    account access at the end of the notice period.
  </p>

  <h2>Project work</h2>
  <p>
    If you cancel a project before it is delivered, you are billed for the work completed up to the
    date we receive your notice. Any advance beyond that is returned. Once a project has been
    delivered and accepted, the fee is not refundable.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising spend</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Advertising spend is never refundable by us.</strong> It is paid to Meta, Google or
    another platform, not to Tisvia Marketing. Refunds for platform spend are a matter between you
    and that platform. We will pause campaigns as soon as you ask.
  </p>

  <h2>Performance</h2>
  <p>
    Fees are charged for the work done, not for a result. We do not refund fees because a campaign
    did not reach a particular cost per lead, sales figure or return on ad spend. See the
    <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>If we cannot deliver</h2>
  <p>
    If we end an engagement ourselves, or cannot deliver work you have already paid for, we refund
    the unused portion of your fee in full.
  </p>

  <h2>How refunds are paid</h2>
  <p>
    Approved refunds are sent to the original payment method within <strong>7 to 10 working
    days</strong> of approval. Bank processing times are outside our control. Any transaction or
    gateway charge already deducted by a payment provider is not refundable.
  </p>

  <h2>How to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    Email us, or message us on WhatsApp and follow it with an email so there is a written record.
    Please include your business name and the service you are cancelling. We acknowledge every
    cancellation in writing.
  </p>

  <h2>Disputes</h2>
  <p>
    Raise any billing dispute within 15 days of the invoice date and we will look into it and come
    back to you.
  </p>
</Legal>
